Superpermutation bounds in Lean: lower bounds for 12 and 13 symbols from Theorem C, checked by the kernel (a
Superpermutation Almanac batch)

This project contains Lean sources from four repositories and new files.

Jakub Halfar, superpermutations
https://github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations, commit 64ab6a783731744882bc1886124faaf370fa9223
Apache License 2.0, reproduced in licenses/jhalfar-superpermutations-LICENSE.
Included: the modules of LowerBounds/ that Theorem C needs (from the directory proofs/lean/lower), the modules
of Superperm/ (from proofs/lean/words) and the generators tools/s_plan2.py and tools/s_ksim.py (from
proofs/lean/lower/tools, unchanged). One file was changed for the Almanac and says so at its top:
LowerBounds/SSearch.lean (a local macro written as a local notation with the same expansion).

Zach Hunter and Uku Raudvere, superpermutations-hunter
https://github.com/urdvr/superpermutations-hunter, commit d45222190031d162feb1f6f3cf5fe2d11fab726d
Apache License 2.0, reproduced in licenses/hunter-superpermutations-hunter-LICENSE.
Included: the 75 modules of Hunter/ that the proof imports.
Hunter/ProofsGreedy.lean and Hunter/ProofsGreedy2.lean were changed for Lean 4.35.0 and the Mathlib commit
56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679 (proof steps only); each says at its top what was changed.

